      "content": "Both options have their merits, but I would recommend considering a conditional lottery system that prioritizes those with the highest need. This approach would allocate a portion of units based on income, while reserving a smaller percentage for individuals living near transit hubs to ensure proximity benefits are not entirely reserved for those who can afford it. Additionally, you could also consider offering tiered preferences, allowing applicants with higher needs to register early, to maximize fairness and accessibility.",
